From 3cf535aa67ea29a1df4a0bded0428bddac49761e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:13:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sidebar: show a thread waiting for an answer to the agent's
 question

The sidebar had a status for an agent waiting on a *permission* -- the
yellow warning triangle -- and none for an agent waiting on an *answer*. When
the agent asks a question (an `AskUserQuestion` form, which reaches Zed as a
session-scoped elicitation), the turn stays open while it waits, so the row
showed the grey running spinner: it read as "still working" while the thread
was in fact blocked on the user.

The pieces were already here. `Conversation` has kept an
`elicitation_requests` map, fed by `ElicitationRequested` and
`ElicitationResponded`, since upstream added session-scoped elicitations --
and nothing read it. The sidebar's `WaitingForConfirmation` is computed from
`permission_requests` alone (`pending_tool_call`), which is why a question
never reached it.

What this adds:

- `AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForAnswer`, drawn with IconName::Chat tinted
  Accent and a "Waiting for Your Answer" tooltip. A separate status rather
  than the warning triangle, because the two ask different things of the user:
  a permission takes one click, a question takes reading and writing.
- `Conversation::has_pending_elicitation`, read through
  `ConversationView::root_thread_has_pending_elicitation`. Like
  `pending_tool_call` it spans the root thread and its subagents, so a
  subagent's question marks its parent's row.
- Ranking: a permission outranks a question (the one-click unblock is the
  cheaper thing to show first), and a question outranks error, background and
  running, as the permission already did.
- `register_thread` now seeds pending questions the way it already seeded
  pending permissions. A thread that was asked a question before the
  conversation registered it never emits `ElicitationRequested` again, and
  without the seed it would read as running until answered.
- "Stop" and the archive guard treat it like the other waiting state: the turn
  is still open, so stopping it is meaningful and archiving it is not.

What it deliberately does not do: the collapsed project header's badge still
counts permissions only ("N threads are waiting for confirmation"); a question
is not a confirmation, and folding it into that text would make it wrong.

Pure Zed: elicitations are generic ACP, so any agent that asks a form-mode
question gets the status. Rides the claude-agent-acp-plus flag BY CHOICE, like
0010/0012/0014/0026/0027, next to 0029, whose status list it extends.

(0.2.3_p20261009): the sidebar row's status is `thread_row_status`, a pure function with a
truth table -- a permission prompt outranks a question, both outrank an error,
background work marks only an idle thread. A subagent's open question keeps the
conversation waiting, and answering it clears that.
---

